cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this proof and Lean formalization when using or discussing this result."
title: "Glushkov's L/X problem: exact directed diameter of the symmetric group in Lean 4"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Uskov
    given-names: S.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-5845-7013"
  - family-names: Chervov
    given-names: A.
  - family-names: Levkovich-Maslyuk
    given-names: F.
  - family-names: Litvak
    given-names: I.
  - family-names: Smolensky
    given-names: A.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-28
repository-code: "https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean"
url: "https://github.com/snow-ghost/glushkov-lx-lean"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of the exact directed Cayley diameter of S_n
  generated by a cyclic shift L and the transposition X of the first two
  positions, for all n >= 5. The diameter is (3*n^2-8*n+9)/4 for odd n
  and (3*n^2-8*n+12)/4 for even n. Includes upper and lower bounds,
  a literal-word routing theorem, and an audit of axioms in the local
  import closure.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal proof
  - Cayley graphs
  - symmetric group
  - directed diameter
  - A039745
